{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792667756,"nonce":"yCUsjD8N+X4lYCjnBhTyCcZ08bo=","message":"**M3 handover** (branch b768fbb-m3-plan-with-wtx, HEAD e465feb)\n\n**What M3 does**\n- Start at step 3 (ready, normal risk, no plan) runs `wtx go \u003cbranch\u003e --prompt F --no-attach` with step 3's prompt. The prompt asks for the plan in plan mode, then, once it is accepted in the pane: commit it as `\u003cplans\u003e/\u003cissue\u003e-\u003cslug\u003e.md` with `issue:` and `status: draft` in its front matter, push, open a draft PR, and stop. The status stays ready. With `plans-in-pr = false` the prompt says no PR at this step.\n- Start work at low risk (or with the plan already approved) moves the status to in-progress and runs `wtx go` with step 4's prompt.\n- Approve posts `plan:approve`, moves the status to in-progress, then briefs the agent through `wtx brief` (only once a plan file exists; with no plan there is nothing to accept, and the server would refuse with no-plan).\n- Revise is the comment plus `wtx brief`, as before.\n- Step 3 shows the strip (worktree, agent state, draft PR link), the plan's meta (path, issue, status), and the approver's sentence. The draft PR shows on step 3's line and in the status bar. In-progress with a draft PR waits for it to be marked ready, and in-review with a draft PR offers no review.\n- The server adds no `git push` or `gh` surface. The agent pushes and opens the draft PR itself.\n\n**Not done: the live half of Done-when**\nChecked on a local scratch clone with a fake wtx: the go/brief argv, the prompts, the status moves, and the page at 1440px and 900px against C3/C4. Not checked:\n- A real `wtx go`: the sandbox refuses tmux (`error creating /private/tmp/tmux-502/...: Operation not permitted`).\n- The draft PR and `gh pr ready`: pointing the scratch clone at GitHub was denied. The strip's draft PR link has no test and no live run, so this check is its only coverage.\n\nTo check by hand, on a git-board-test clone with a `risk` field, serving this branch:\n1. A ready issue with criteria and normal risk. Press Start, then accept the plan in the agent's pane.\n2. The agent commits the plan, pushes, and opens the draft PR. The page should show the strip's draft link and \"draft PR #N\" on step 3's line (within the 5 minute PR cache).\n3. Approve. Accept again in the pane (see `--build` below). The agent writes and pushes the test.\n4. `gh pr ready N`. The \"Mark ready for review\" action appears, then Review at in-review.\n\n**Your call: wtx `brief --build`**\nNot made. The `buildBrief` constant in internal/server/worktrees.go stays false. `wtx brief` always restarts the pane in plan mode, so Approve and Revise restart the planner and the person accepts in the pane again. \"Approve takes the agent out of plan mode\" is therefore not delivered yet. The proposed wtx change, for a paired worktree of EPFL-ENAC/wtx:\n- cli.py: `brief --build`, and `cmd_brief` passes `phase=\"build\"`.\n- tmux.py:312: thread the phase through `ensure_session` instead of the hardcoded `\"plan\" if brief`.\n- `PLAN_INSTRUCTION` only for plan briefs. Effort `orch.build_effort`.\n- One test in wtx.\nThen flip `buildBrief` to true.\n\n**Rulings made here**\n- The draft note shows at step 5 only. At step 4 a draft PR is the step's own state (C4).\n- The approver's words: \"You approve\", else \"\u003clogin\u003e approves\", else \"The plan role approves\". The brief says \"approved by \u003clogin\u003e\" only when the approval has a login.\n\n**Deferred on purpose**\n- C3's plan versions (v1/v2, \"Changes since v1\", Edit): the plan's git history, worth its own item.\n- \"Open the session\" (nothing a browser can open), and parsing wtx's handoff record.\n- `plans-in-pr = false`: the plan stays on the branch, and the PR waits until step 5.\n- Structural risk at step 3 uses the same plan prompt. Structural plans normally go on a `plan/` branch PR.\n\n**Seen, not this branch's**\n- \"Approved by \" with an empty login: cycle.ts:91, CyclePlan.vue:29 (from M2).\n- \"Approve the plan\" and \"Ask the agent to revise\" are offered with no plan file. Approve with no plan now only moves the status, with no brief.\n- At 900px the header's \"Inbox\" and \"Send 1\" overlap.\n- On a scratch board, inbox follow answers 409 and environments 404.\n- `make ci` fails on TestIssueSyncTakesTheAssigneesMode (issuesync_test.go:92) and TestForgeSyncSetsTheAssigneesMode (assignable_test.go:152). Both fail on main locally too, and main's last three CI runs on GitHub are red (latest 39757059050). The branch doesn't touch those files. Web: typecheck clean, 163/163 tests.\n\n**For M4 to M6**\n- M4: step 4's prompt names the kind's rule. `[cycle.tests]` and `[cycle.checks]` slot in where the prompt's gate is built (worktrees.go, `cyc.Gate`).\n- M5: step 3 lives in CyclePlan.vue. IssueStep.vue only passes `agent` and handles `@approve` and the Start-work button.\n- M6: steps 2, 5 and 7 untouched.","files":null}]}